#: ../../../reference/interfaces/removable-media-interface.md:0
msgid ""
"Reference documentation for the removable-media interface, which grants "
"snaps read and write access to mounted removable storage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/removable-media-interface.md:8
msgid "removable-media interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/removable-media-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"`removable-media` allows read/write access to mounted removable storage in `/"
"media`, `/run/media` and `/mnt`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/removable-media-interface.md:12
msgid ""
"For example, this interface can be used to provide access to mounted USB "
"sticks and external hard drives from the desktop environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/removable-media-interface.md:14
msgid ""
"Security-conscious users may want to remove sensitive external media when "
"installing snaps, before disconnecting the interface from those snaps to "
"prevent them from having access when the data is restored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/removable-media-interface.md:16
msgid "Access to `/mnt` requires snapd version *2.36+*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/removable-media-interface.md:20
msgid "**Auto-connect**: no"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/removable-media-interface.md:22
msgid ""
"This interface is typically {ref}`not granted <interfaces-process-for-"
"aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks>` the ability to {ref}`auto-connect "
"<explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>` because doing so will "
"permit access to potentially sensitive data such as photos, documents and "
"encryption keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/removable-media-interface.md:24
msgid ""
"Certain application types may be granted an exception for the following "
"reasons:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/removable-media-interface.md:26
msgid ""
"**major browsers**: typically designed with security and user privacy in mind"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/removable-media-interface.md:27
msgid ""
"**media editors**: often used to import/edit/export large files on external "
"devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/removable-media-interface.md:28
msgid ""
"**media players/viewers**: often used to import/preview/playback files on "
"external devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/removable-media-interface.md:29
msgid ""
"**media recorders**: often used to export/edit files on external devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/removable-media-interface.md:31
msgid ""
"`removable-media` is considered a _transitional_ interface because, when "
"connected, only traditional UNIX permissions are considered for file access. "
"This allows a background service in a snap to setup _inotify_, for example, "
"to monitor, catalogue and modify files on external media."
msgstr ""
